    },
    "body": "Recorded at the owner's request after a session review, and it corrects my own framing rather than any measurement. The pointer's attention is a softmax over sources (geometric_stack.rs:88-90, :8463, :1053) and the control layer is RoPE softmax attention (:27). Geometry is in the SCORE (lorentz, prime routes); the normalisation and mixture are not geometric. D11 forbids float and transcendentals in served kernels so exp/log-sum-exp cannot be served at all, and export refuses a pointer with an identity term for want of an integer port - so the line is offline-only, which the entries say, but they present it in the same register as the serving work. A capability gain on an unservable mechanism is not progress toward the served model. Also narrows the recorded VSA negative to the fixed token-id-hash codebook implementation it actually measured, rather than the geometry as a family. Unchanged: the served chat stack at 0.93277 BPB, D11 vs D10 exact on 16,384 targets, integer vs float +0.0077 nats, 0.8802 top-1. References #2029",
